Ok, cool.  For the record, you need the following to calculate a full
and accurate score, in rough order of importance:

Xp gained from kills
How the game ended (quit, ascended, killed)
Artifacts, amulets, and gems
Deepest DL reached
Final and starting amounts of gold
Number of wands IDed by engraving
Number of potions IDed by quaffing
Number of scrolls IDed by reading
Number of squeaky boards oiled
Number of tripe rations eaten
Number of "yuk"s from sinks
Number of oracles and the order in which they were received

It's worth noting that even the list of monsters killed won't
necessarily give an accurate number of Xp gained from those kills, as
the experience value of a monster can change from its base value.  For
instance, if the AC or level of the monster changes, so does its Xp
value.  However, I don't think anyone would have a problem with a
calculation based on base Xp value, since it's more likely to reduce his
actual score than inflate it.  

